<https://example.org/comect-demo/study/SYN-0009> a ex:Study ;
    dct:abstract "A completed follow-up cohort examines prolonged symptoms, immune markers and care experiences among adults after infection. This is a wholly fictional observational research example designed to illustrate how a completed machine-actionable data management plan can be discovered alongside other study descriptions. The fictional coordinating institution is Alpine Translational Recovery Centre. Its study countries are Germany, Austria; these locations indicate where the study takes place and do not automatically describe the geographical coverage of any future published dataset. The study is labelled completed at the time of the example. Dates refer to the study plan, not to trial registration or metadata publication. The central scientific question concerns previous symptomatic viral infection. The investigators observe people or records under a defined study protocol rather than assigning a new treatment as the primary research design. The target population includes Adults, Older adults. The description of eligibility is simplified for the demonstration, and any real version would require precise inclusion and exclusion criteria, site approvals, risk assessment and a scientifically justified recruitment strategy. The planned enrolment is 1400 and the achieved or currently recorded enrolment is 1350 in this invented submission. These illustrative figures are not observed research results and should not be used for epidemiological inference. Research activities are represented through setting categories such as Clinic (outpatient), Community. The maDMP records data categories including Serology, Samples and primary outcome categories including Life impact, Physicological or Clinical. This structured metadata is useful for identifying related research, comparing study scope and noticing differences in data collection practices. It is not equivalent to access to clinical records, laboratory measurements or individual participant information. Selected existing records will also be reused, so source descriptions, linkage procedures, provenance and responsible governance would need to be documented before any secondary analysis. A real investigator would also describe missing-data management, audit trails, versioning, documentation and responsible stewardship at each participating institution. The completed form reports standards such as SNOMED CT, LOINC. Selecting these names means the researcher says they use or plan to use them; conformance cannot be established from a checkbox alone. The reported intention is that de-identified participant-level data are already shared in the fictional scenario, but access conditions still have to be reviewed and approval cannot be assumed. Data access questions must be considered separately from study discovery because consent language, retention periods, transfer limitations and data access committees can impose additional requirements. In this demonstration, the purpose of collecting the maDMP is to enable transparent searching for studies and potential collaborators, while preserving enough context to ask informed questions before any data-sharing negotiation. All people, identifiers, funders and organisations described here are fabricated for safe testing." ;
